---
description: Nx monorepo rules for app boundaries, shared libraries, and scalable project structure
alwaysApply: true
---

- This project is an Nx monorepo.
- Keep frontend and backend as separate apps.
- Keep apps independently runnable when required.
- Prefer shared libraries only for stable, reusable, cross-cutting concerns.
- Do not move code to shared libraries prematurely.
- Avoid circular dependencies across apps and libraries.
- Keep feature ownership explicit.
- Favor predictable structure over clever abstractions.

Recommended structure:
- apps/front-end
- apps/back-end
- libs/shared-types only if truly reused
- libs/shared-utils only if truly reused
- libs/ui only if truly reused
- libs/config only if truly reused

Frontend:
- Organize by feature under src/features.
- Keep routing and layouts under src/app.
- Keep shared UI, hooks, and utilities under src/shared only when reused by multiple features.

Backend:
- Organize by domain module under src.
- Keep common concerns under src/common.
- Keep config centralized.
- Keep migrations explicit.

Nx targets:
- Prefer independent targets for lint, test, build, e2e, and serve.
- Prefer frontend and backend pipelines to run independently.

- If the challenge scope does not require a shared library, do not create one just to improve perceived architecture.